  "party_positions": [
    {
      "claims": [
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Shanmugam",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "b6d95fd705c30e3e4949478a941ad1732bc3e16371c034b458d3b6e7abdf4ee7",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-b6d95fd705c3-0001-0003"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 31,
                "start": 31
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Shanmugam, goldman contends that the Second Circuit failed to apply the guidance from *Amgen* and *Halliburton II* regarding consideration of all relevant evidence."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Goldman",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "f63bb538fd6b0a9af67d4588b3d65fef090ae457a7503196b09e822b7e304129",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-f63bb538fd6b-0001-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 13,
                "start": 13
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "Goldman argues that the Second Circuit erred by requiring Goldman, rather than Plaintiffs, to bear the burden of persuasion on price impact at class certification."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Goldman",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "f63bb538fd6b0a9af67d4588b3d65fef090ae457a7503196b09e822b7e304129",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-f63bb538fd6b-0001-0002"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 13,
                "start": 13
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Goldman, goldman relies on Federal Rule of Evidence 301, which places the burden of producing evidence to rebut a presumption on the party against whom the presumption is directed, but does not shift the burden of persuasion."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Goldman",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "f63bb538fd6b0a9af67d4588b3d65fef090ae457a7503196b09e822b7e304129",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-f63bb538fd6b-0001-0007"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 17,
                "start": 17
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "Goldman contends that general statements, like those at issue, cannot affect a company\u2019s stock price because they are too general for a reasonable investor to rely upon."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Goldman",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "f63bb538fd6b0a9af67d4588b3d65fef090ae457a7503196b09e822b7e304129",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-f63bb538fd6b-0000-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 6,
                "start": 6
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "Goldman argues that the Second Circuit erred twice: first, by holding that the generic nature of the alleged misrepresentations is irrelevant to the price\u2011impact inquiry; and second, by assigning Goldman the burden of persuasion to prove a lack of price impact."
        }
      ],
